WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.290
My phone was in my bag on

2
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.170
the bus this morning.

3
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.780
Now it’s gone.

4
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.180
It has the class groups, pupils’ phone

5
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.000
numbers and photos of their marks.

6
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.050
Where do I even start?

7
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.800
Today: what to do when school data

8
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.720
goes wrong, step by step.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.140
A data incident is any time

10
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.980
personal data is lost, stolen or

11
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.300
seen by the wrong people.

12
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.700
A lost phone.

13
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.060
Marks sent to the wrong group.

14
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.970
A hacked email sending scams.

15
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.870
A USB stick with exam papers,

16
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.290
left in a cyber café.

17
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.060
When it happens, follow five steps.

18
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.090
Contain it, so the damage stops spreading.

19
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.350
Report it the same day.

20
00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.870
Assess what data it was, and whose.

21
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.210
Notify the people affected.

22
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.190
Then learn, so it doesn’t happen again.

23
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.900
Containing comes first, and fast.

24
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.340
Delete a wrong message for everyone, and

25
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.960
ask people to delete their copies.

26
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.010
Lock or erase a lost phone

27
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:06.830
from another device.

28
00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.710
Change the passwords.

29
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.770
Unplug an infected

30
00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.910
computer from the network.

31
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.590
It’s like a burst pipe in a classroom.

32
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.260
First you turn off the water.

33
00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.270
Then you tell the caretaker, check what

34
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.950
got wet, and warn whoever uses the room.

35
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.750
Later, you fix the pipe so it

36
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:27.510
doesn’t burst again.

37
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:29.230
Quick check!

38
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.200
You’ve just sent the class marks list

39
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.940
to the parents’ group by mistake.

40
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.940
What do you do first?

41
00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.130
Delete it for everyone right away, then

42
00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.990
tell the head teacher the same day.

43
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.140
Ask parents who saw it to delete it too.

44
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.150
Telling quickly isn’t a confession:

45
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.450
it’s what keeps the damage small.

46
00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.110
Next, the school leader assesses.

47
00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.630
What data was it, and whose?

48
00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.770
How much harm could it do?

49
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.640
If it’s serious, the people affected are

50
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.000
told, and often the regulator too.

51
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.200
Many laws set a deadline, often

52
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.900
seventy-two hours, so report early

53
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.360
and let your leader decide.

54
00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.310
A few things never help.

55
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.360
Don’t hide it, and don’t delete the

56
00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.200
evidence: screenshots help.

57
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.260
Don’t pay anyone who demands money.

58
00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.690
And don’t argue with an

59
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.210
attacker: report them.

60
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.950
Many incidents start with a call or

61
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.150
a message asking for a code.

62
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.270
In the lab, take a call from “IT

63
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.170
support”, and choose what to say.

64
00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:38.830
Your turn.

65
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.500
My email has started sending

66
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.140
scam messages to parents.

67
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.080
Which step comes first?

68
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.380
Contain it first: change the password and

69
00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.100
sign out everywhere, then warn parents.

70
00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.340
Remember the five steps, contain,

71
00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.260
report, assess, notify and learn, and

72
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.180
report early, without blame.

73
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.970
Try it in class tomorrow: give groups a

74
00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.290
card each, a lost phone, a photo sent to

75
00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.430
the wrong group, a hacked game account.

76
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.710
Each group decides the first

77
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.710
thing to do, and who to tell.
